{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Howzit. Contraception clinic is through there. Doctor's running late, the computer's been sulking all morning. Take a seat and sister will call you.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, cool. I'm not in a rush.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): We parked by the robot, took forever. Come, let's sit.",
  "[SEG0004] person_4 (NURSE): Right, come in. I'm doing your blood pressure before you see the doctor.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag, is that even necessary? I'm fine.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (NURSE): Blood pressure is 118 over 74, pulse is 72. That's a nice reading.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (NURSE): My sister had the implant put in last year after her baby, and I've got blood pressure myself so I don't mess about with these checks.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm. Ok.",
  "[SEG0009] person_4 (NURSE): You can go through. Mom can come if you want.",
  "[SEG0010] person_5 (DOCTOR): Sorry, one second, this screen has frozen again. Right. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): I need something for contraception. That's it.",
  "[SEG0012] person_5 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say that again? I clicked the wrong thing.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): Contraception. I was on the pill and it gave me headaches so I chucked it.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Doctor, she was on Yasminne, no, Yasmin. Those headaches went on for about three months. She was missing shifts.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag mom, no. It was like two weeks and then it was gone. I still went to work. It was nothing.",
  "[SEG0016] person_5 (DOCTOR): Yasmin, you said? Hang on, the cursor's jumped. One tablet?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, Yasmin, one tablet every day. I stopped it.",
  "[SEG0018] person_5 (DOCTOR): When did you stop?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Err. A few months ago. I can't remember the month, um, maybe March, no, I actually don't know.",
  "[SEG0020] person_5 (DOCTOR): And you're sure the headaches are finished?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja. Gone. It was just a sore head.",
  "[SEG0022] person_5 (DOCTOR): Before the pain, any flashing lights, zigzags, that sort of thing?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm, I suppose. Sometimes. Not really.",
  "[SEG0024] person_5 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Occasionally. At a braai. Not every day. It's not a thing.",
  "[SEG0026] person_5 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines? Sorry, repeat that if I look down, I'm opening your file.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing I know of.",
  "[SEG0028] person_5 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0030] person_5 (DOCTOR): Family side, diabetes, blood pressure, hearts?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja my dad had diabetes in his fifties, my mom didn't have any of that, my older sister's got high blood pressure but no sugar, and my uncle on my dad's side had a heart attack.",
  "[SEG0032] person_5 (DOCTOR): And day to day, work and the rest? Say it slowly, I'm typing.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): I work at a call centre in Rosebank, hours are eight till five, sometimes I stay till seven if the queue's mad. Diet is whatever, pap and chicken or takeaways from the garage. Exercise, ag I don't really, maybe a walk if the robot's far. Alcohol, weekends, a few ciders, not during the week.",
  "[SEG0034] person_5 (DOCTOR): Ok. So what happens is the oestrogen in the combined pill can make the blood a bit thicker, and the vessels in the head react, that's where the headache comes from. With you smoking, even now and then, I don't want you back on a combined pill. The clot risk climbs.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja well, the headaches were nothing, but ok, whatever you say.",
  "[SEG0036] person_5 (DOCTOR): My working impression is those headaches were from the Yasmin, not a separate migraine thing. We can look at the implant, the injection, or a copper coil. None of those have oestrogen.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): The implant, maybe. I don't know. I'm not fussed.",
  "[SEG0038] person_5 (DOCTOR): Sister, can you give her the implant leaflet?",
  "[SEG0039] person_4 (NURSE): Here, Implanon leaflet. My own boy is only four, so I'm not choosing this for myself, but people like having it on paper.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): I'll read it at the flat. Not deciding today.",
  "[SEG0041] person_5 (DOCTOR): Good. Nothing starts today, and don't fetch any pills from the chemist in the meantime. We'll book you back in two weeks and you can tell me what you've picked.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I can book the two weeks at the front. Morning?",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (PATIENT): Morning, ja. I won't get any. Thanks.",
  "[SEG0044] person_5 (DOCTOR): Sharp. See you then."
 ],
